findings.fix:
Reject the empty string and validate every character including word[0]:

  bool IsNum(const string word) {
      if (word.empty()) return false;
      for (unsigned int i = 0; i < word.length(); i++) {
          if (!isdigit((unsigned char)word[i])) return false;
      }
      return true;
  }

(Multi-char words are unaffected: IsNum("2res") stays false, IsNum("201") stays true, and identifiers are still caught earlier by IsIdentifier, so the reference token table is unchanged.)

Require non-word boundaries around the match before emitting a position, e.g. inside the while loop:

  bool leftOk  = (col == 0) || (!isalnum((unsigned char)line[col-1]) && line[col-1] != '_');
  string::size_type end = col + value.length();
  bool rightOk = (end >= line.length()) || (!isalnum((unsigned char)line[end]) && line[end] != '_');
  if (leftOk && rightOk) position << "第" << row << "行第" << col << "列";

This keeps the existing 0-based column convention that the reference output uses.

